README.OSK -- LFCRMan, from the OS-9 International code diskWolfgang Ocker's LFCRMan, a file manager that shows an existing RBF or NFSdevice with its line endings translated between LF and CR, printed inOS-9 International issue 2/93 ("Sharing text files via NFS", page 9) anddistributed on the magazine's code disk by EFFO.CMDS/DRIVERS holds the three modules the code disk built: lfcrman (thefile manager), and h0t and thlpct, two example descriptors.  h0t presents/h0 as /h0t; thlpct presents a device named /thlpc as/thlpct.  Both name `null' as their driver, which is Microware's; LFCRMandoes the work itself and needs no driver of its own.Changes: none to any file shipped.  Three files of the code disk are NOThere:  path.h     Microware's DEFS/path.h (94% of its lines are theirs) with an             lfcr_pvt member added to the private-data union.  Your own             DEFS/path.h plus that member is what lfcrman.c includes.  netdesc.a  the descriptor macro file h0t.a and thlpct.a use; it is built             on Microware's device-descriptor template (47% of its lines             match their nulldesc.a).  The two descriptors ship built.  netdriv.a  a do-nothing driver ("pssdriv"), marked "All Rights Reserved!",             which the makefile does not build.Not tested.  The emulator used for this collection loads no file managers.